STUDENT AI AGENT
Complete Build, Test, Deploy and Web Integration Guide
Strands Agents • Amazon Bedrock AgentCore • Lambda • DynamoDB • S3 • CloudFront
Final outcome  A working chat.html hosted in a private S3 bucket and delivered over HTTPS by CloudFront. The browser calls StudentAgentProxy Lambda, which invokes the deployed AgentCore Runtime. The Strands agent calls StudentLookupTool Lambda, which queries DynamoDB.



1. What we are building
Layer	Service / technology	Responsibility
Browser UI	chat.html (HTML/CSS/JavaScript)	Captures questions and displays answers.
Static hosting	Private S3 bucket + CloudFront OAC	Stores chat.html and serves it over HTTPS.
Browser API	Lambda Function URL	HTTPS endpoint called by the browser.
Proxy	StudentAgentProxy Lambda	Validates input, retains session ID and invokes AgentCore.
Agent runtime	Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime	Runs the deployed Strands StudentAgent.
Tool adapter	StudentLookupTool Lambda	Queries DynamoDB using ClassScoreIndex.
Data	DynamoDB StudentRecords	Stores synthetic student records.

Browser (CloudFront HTTPS)
    |
    | POST { message, sessionId }
    v
StudentAgentProxy Lambda Function URL
    |
    | bedrock-agentcore:InvokeAgentRuntime (AWS SDK / IAM)
    v
Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime
    |
    | Strands student_lookup tool -> lambda.invoke
