Required tools: AWS CLI v2, Node.js 20+, npm, Python 3.12, uv, and the npm AgentCore CLI. Docker is not required for the agent-python-strands CodeZip template.
The AWS identity must be allowed to create IAM roles/policies, DynamoDB tables, Lambda functions, AgentCore resources, S3 buckets and CloudFront distributions. The account must be allowed to invoke the selected Bedrock inference profile.
Terminal/session rule: keep the main deployment commands in one Bash terminal so exported variables remain available. If you open a new terminal, re-run the AWS Region and account exports from Step 2. After deployment, re-run the Runtime discovery commands in Step 17 before creating the proxy role.



